.TH NGSPICE-DOCKER-PYTHON 1 "March 2026" "IHP macOS Toolkit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ngspice-docker-python \- Intelligent ngspice wrapper for Python integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ngspice-docker-python
[\fB\-b\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIlogfile\fR]
.I netlist.sp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ngspice-docker-python
is an enhanced wrapper around ngspice-docker that provides intelligent path
translation for Python tools like mosplot and IHP-AnalogAcademy.

Unlike the basic ngspice-docker wrapper, this version:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Parses SPICE netlists to find path references
.IP \(bu 2
Automatically translates macOS paths to Docker container paths
.IP \(bu 2
Handles .include, .lib, pre_osdi, and write statements
.IP \(bu 2
Manages dynamic Docker volume mounts
.IP \(bu 2
Cleans up temporary files
.RE
.PP
This wrapper is specifically designed for programmatic use by Python tools
that generate netlists with absolute macOS paths.
.SH PREREQUISITES
Same as
.BR ngspice-docker (1):
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Environment configured (source zshrc_elec)
.IP \(bu 2
Docker Desktop running
.IP \(bu 2
TOOLKIT_ROOT and PDK_ROOT set
.RE
.PP
Additionally required for Python integration:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3.9+
.IP \(bu 2
Virtual environment with gmid/mosplot (optional)
.RE
.SH USAGE
.SS From Command Line
Same syntax as ngspice-docker:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
ngspice-docker-python -b netlist.sp
.EE
.in
.SS From Python (mosplot)
The wrapper is automatically invoked by mosplot when configured:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
from mosplot.lookup_table_generator.simulators import NgspiceSimulator

ngspice = NgspiceSimulator(
    simulator_path="ngspice-docker-python",
    lib_mappings=[...],
    ...
)
.EE
.in
.SS From Python (IHP-AnalogAcademy)
Configure in academy scripts:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
ngspice = NgspiceSimulator(
    simulator_path="ngspice-docker-python",
    ...
)
.EE
.in
.SH PATH TRANSLATION
The wrapper intelligently translates paths in these SPICE statements:
.TP
.B .include
.EX
.include /Users/you/project/models.lib
→ .include /work/models.lib
.EE
.TP
.B .lib
.EX
.lib /Users/you/PDK/models.lib section
→ .lib /pdk/models.lib section
.EE
.TP
.B pre_osdi
.EX
pre_osdi /Users/you/models/device.osdi
→ pre_osdi /pdk/models/device.osdi
.EE
.TP
.B write
.EX
write /tmp/tmpXXX/output.txt
→ write /work/tmp/tmpXXX/output.txt
.EE
.PP
And handles -o flag:
.EX
ngspice-docker-python -o /tmp/log.txt netlist.sp
→ mounts /tmp and translates path
.EE
.SH DYNAMIC VOLUME MOUNTS
The wrapper analyzes the netlist and dynamically mounts only necessary volumes:
.PP
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Path Pattern|Mount Point
_
$PDK_ROOT/*|/pdk (read-only)
$(pwd)/*|/work (read-write)
/tmp/*|/tmp (read-write)
$TMPDIR/*|Temporary mount
.TE
.PP
This minimizes Docker overhead and security exposure.
.SH TEMPORARY FILES
The wrapper creates a modified netlist with translated paths:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
/tmp/ngspice_XXXXXX.sp
.EE
.in
.PP
This file is automatically cleaned up after simulation, even if ngspice fails.
.SH DIFFERENCES FROM NGSPICE-DOCKER
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
Feature|ngspice-docker|ngspice-docker-python
_
Path translation|Basic|Intelligent parsing
Volume mounts|Fixed|Dynamic
Python integration|Manual|Automatic
Netlist parsing|No|Yes
Cleanup|Manual|Automatic
Use case|Interactive|Programmatic
.TE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Manual Use
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Works like ngspice-docker
ngspice-docker-python -b circuit.sp
.EE
.in
.SS With mosplot
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# In your Python script
ngspice = NgspiceSimulator(
    simulator_path="ngspice-docker-python",
    include_paths=[model_path],
    ...
)

# mosplot generates netlists with macOS paths
# Wrapper translates automatically
lookup_table = generator.build("output")
.EE
.in
.SS With IHP-AnalogAcademy
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# In academy module scripts
ngspice = NgspiceSimulator(
    simulator_path="ngspice-docker-python",
    lib_mappings=[(model_path, "mos_tt")],
    ...
)

# Academy scripts work without modification
.EE
.in
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.SS Wrapper not found by Python
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Ensure toolkit is in PATH before activating venv
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/projets/env/zshrc_elec
source $ASIC_DESIGN_ROOT/outils/venv_ihp/bin/activate

# Verify
which ngspice-docker-python
.EE
.in
.SS Path translation issues
.PP
Enable debug mode by editing the wrapper script:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Add at top of wrapper
set -x  # Enable bash debugging
.EE
.in
.PP
Then check stdout for path translations.
.SS Docker volume errors
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Verify paths exist and are readable
ls -la $PDK_ROOT
ls -la $(pwd)

# Check Docker has access
docker run --rm -v "$PDK_ROOT:/pdk" alpine ls /pdk
.EE
.in
.SS Temporary file not cleaned
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Manual cleanup if needed
rm /tmp/ngspice_*.sp
.EE
.in
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Same as
.BR ngspice-docker (1),
plus:
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Optional. Specifies temporary directory for intermediate files.
If not set, uses /tmp.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/ngspice-docker-python
The wrapper script (Python-aware)
.TP
.I $TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/ngspice-docker
Base wrapper (called internally)
.TP
.I /tmp/ngspice_*.sp
Temporary netlists with translated paths (auto-cleanup)
.SH PERFORMANCE
The intelligent parsing adds ~50-100ms overhead compared to ngspice-docker.
This is negligible for typical simulations (seconds to minutes).
